JOURNAL_REQUEST


REQ_ID	NUMBER	No		1	
REQ_STATUS	VARCHAR2(10 CHAR)	No	'P' 	2	Row-level processing status (e.g., P for Pending, A for Approved, R for Rejected).
REQ_DATE	DATE	No	SYSDATE 	3	
CREATOR_ID	VARCHAR2(12 CHAR)	No		4	
EXECUTOR_ID	VARCHAR2(12 CHAR)	Yes		5	User ID of the person who processed this specific row.
EXECUTION_DATE	DATE	Yes		6	Timestamp when this specific row was processed.
EXECUTOR_REMARKS	VARCHAR2(50 CHAR)	Yes		7	Remarks provided by the executor applied to this specific row.
BATCH_ID	VARCHAR2(50 CHAR)	Yes		8	Foreign key linking this row to its parent in JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.
JOURNAL_ID	VARCHAR2(50 CHAR)	Yes		9	Unique identifier for the individual request.
COMMON_BATCH_REMARKS	VARCHAR2(50 CHAR)	Yes		10	Remarks inherited from the batch creation process.
REQ_BRANCH_CODE	VARCHAR2(50 BYTE)	Yes		11	The branch code requested for the transaction.
REQ_CURRENCY	VARCHAR2(3 BYTE)	Yes		12	The 3-character currency code requested.
REQ_CGL	VARCHAR2(50 BYTE)	Yes		13	The 10-digit CGL account code requested.
REQ_AMOUNT	NUMBER(25,4)	Yes		14	Raw requested amount 
REQ_CSV_DATE	DATE	Yes		15	The transaction date provided in the uploaded file.
REQ_NARRATION	VARCHAR2(200 BYTE)	Yes		16	remarks from the uploaded file.
REQ_PRODUCT	VARCHAR2(50 BYTE)	Yes		17	The product  code requested.
CHANGE_TYPE	VARCHAR2(10 CHAR)	Yes		18	
CREATOR_ROLE	NUMBER(10,0)	Yes		19	
PAYLOAD	CLOB	Yes		20	


JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER

BATCH_ID	VARCHAR2(50 BYTE)	No		1	Unique identifier for the uploaded batch file.
CREATOR_ID	VARCHAR2(50 BYTE)	Yes		2	User ID of the person who upload/create the batch.
REQ_DATE	TIMESTAMP(6)	Yes		3	Timestamp when the batch was originally created.
BATCH_REMARKS	VARCHAR2(200 BYTE)	Yes		4	Initial remarks provided by the creator upon create.
TOTAL_ROWS	NUMBER	Yes	0	5	Total number of valid transaction rows contained in this batch.
TOTAL_DEBIT	NUMBER(25,4)	Yes	0	6	Sum of all debit transaction amounts in the batch.
TOTAL_CREDIT	NUMBER(25,4)	Yes	0	7	Sum of all credit transaction amounts in the batch.
BATCH_STATUS	VARCHAR2(20 BYTE)	Yes		8	Current workflow state (e.g., PENDING, ACCEPTED, REJECTED, ERROR).
EXECUTOR_ID	VARCHAR2(50 BYTE)	Yes		9	User ID of the person who approved or rejected the batch.
EXECUTION_DATE	TIMESTAMP(6)	Yes		10	Timestamp when the batch was approved or rejected.
EXECUTOR_REMARKS	VARCHAR2(200 BYTE)	Yes		11	Remarks provided by the executor when approving or rejecting.

MASTER_JOURNAL

JOURNAL_ID	NUMBER(19,0)	No		1	Unique sequential identifier for the master journal entry.
JOURNAL_AMT	NUMBER(38,2)	Yes		2	Absolute transaction amount. Always positive; Txn Type determines debit/credit.
AR_FLAG	VARCHAR2(1 CHAR)	Yes		3	Status flag indicating the record state. Default is A for Approved/Active.
BATCH_ID	VARCHAR2(50 CHAR)	Yes		4	Reference to the parent batch from JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.
JOURNAL_BRANCH	VARCHAR2(50 CHAR)	Yes		5	The branch code where the transaction is booked.
JOURNAL_CGL	VARCHAR2(50 CHAR)	Yes		6	The 10-digit Common General Ledger (CGL) account code.
COMMON_BATCH_REMARKS	VARCHAR2(50 CHAR)	Yes		7	Batch-level remarks provided by the executor during approval.
CURRENCY	VARCHAR2(3 CHAR)	Yes		8	The 3-character currency code (e.g., INR, USD) for the transaction.
JOURNAL_ID_REF	VARCHAR2(50 CHAR)	Yes		9	Reference back to the original row ID from the JOURNAL_REQUEST staging table.
JOURNAL_PDATE	DATE	Yes		10	CSV date of the journal entry.
PRODUCT_TYPE	VARCHAR2(20 CHAR)	Yes		11	The 8-digit product code
REMARKS	VARCHAR2(50 CHAR)	Yes		12	specific remarks for this individual entry.
TXN_TYPE	VARCHAR2(20 CHAR)	Yes		13	Specifies if the entry is a Debit or Credit.
AC_CLASSIFICATION	VARCHAR2(255 CHAR)	Yes		14	
